# Interface Vision (Cyberpunk Theme)

Sidequest Mail should feel like a cyberpunk operating system — but work like Proton Mail.
The neon glow is the skin, not the mechanics.
Everything below is aesthetic and optional; the core email flow (read, reply, file, delete) must always be instant.

---

## Layout Grid

| Screen       | Cyberpunk Concept          | Behavior                                                                 |
|:-------------|:---------------------------|:-------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| **Inbox**    | The Data Stream            | Emails flow in like data packets. Unread emails pulse with neon light.   |
|              |                            | Opening one "decrypts" it — the glow stabilizes.                         |
| **Folders**  | Secure Vaults              | Each folder is a locked vault. Navigating there shows: *"Vault Accessed."* |
| **Sent**     | Transmission Log           | You sent the data. "Transmission Complete" energy.                       |
| **Trash**    | The Void                   | Where data gets deleted from the grid. Dragging an email there erases it. |
|              |                            | Restoring it is "retrieving from the void."                              |
| **Drafts**   | The Lab                    | Still under construction. Glitching code, half-formed structures.        |

---

## Navigation Grid

| Key          | Action                     | Flavor Text                              |
|:-------------|:---------------------------|:-----------------------------------------|
| **Arrow Keys** | Move focus between emails  | Digital chirp sound effect               |
| **Spacebar**   | Open selected email        | *"Decrypting..."*                        |
| **Enter**      | Reply while reading        | *"Sending transmission."*                |
| **Drag & Drop** | Move between folders       | Data packet transfer animation           |

---

## Visual Design Grid

| Element        | Concept                | Description                                                                 |
|:---------------|:-----------------------|:----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| **Sidebar**    | Neural Interface       | A dark panel with neon accents. Labels look like system commands.            |
| **Email Cards** | Data Packets           | Each email is a sleek panel with sender's name and subject. Unread panels glow. |
| **Compose**    | The Terminal           | A command-line-inspired editor. Subject line = mission briefing.             |
| **Stickers**   | Glitch Art             | Inserting a sticker looks like a data corruption effect or hologram.         |

---

## Micro-interactions Grid

| Action         | Sound / Effect         | Trigger Context                          |
|:---------------|:-----------------------|:-----------------------------------------|
| Reading        | Digital hum            | Like powering up a device                |
| Replying       | Transmission beep      | Like sending a secure message            |
| Deleting       | Glitch noise           | Like data corruption                     |
| Searching      | Scan tone              | Like a scanner locking on                |
| Composing      | Keyboard click         | Like typing on a mechanical keyboard     |
| Loading        | Progress bar           | Fills like a system load meter           |

> All sounds default to **off**, toggleable in Settings → Audio.
> Silent mode is the default for a reason: this is still an email client people use at work.

